      "content": "Special Speed Restrictions"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Competitive exams often test legal speed limits specified for two-wheelers versus heavy commercial vehicles.",
        "Section 183 of the Motor Vehicles Act mandates penalties for driving at speeds exceeding prescribed limits.",
        "Identify the difference between national highway speed caps and local urban speed restrictions."
      ],
      "id": "yc47rth"
    },
    {
      "id": "ef1x9nj",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Near schools, hospitals, and crowded areas — drive very slowly (usually 25–30 km/h)",
        "Speed bumps / road humps — slow down completely before crossing",
        "Night driving on unlit roads — reduce speed significantly",
        "Foggy or rainy conditions — reduce speed and use fog lights/hazard lights",
        "Near railway crossings — slow down and check for trains",
        "Through villages — maximum 25 km/h"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "luhtb74",
      "content": "Note: A speed limit sign on the road overrides the general limit. Always follow the lowest applicable speed limit."
    }
  ],
